From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HOYOUNG SEO <hy50.seo@samsung.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 17:18:34 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 028/117] scsi: ufs: core: Limit early link recovery in the
 error handler to runtime PM

ufshcd_err_handler() recovers the link without taking hba->host_sem
whenever hba->pm_op_in_progress is set. That early path was added by commit
f966e02ae521 ("scsi: ufs: core: Fix runtime suspend error deadlock")
because the regular error handling would wait for a runtime PM operation
that cannot complete while the error handler is waiting.

pm_op_in_progress is also set during system suspend, system resume,
shutdown and poweroff, where the early path is not needed and runs
concurrently with the PM path itself. For example, if a LINERESET is
reported and the hibern8 exit fails in __ufshcd_wl_resume() during system
resume, both ufshcd_err_handler() and __ufshcd_wl_resume() call
ufshcd_link_recovery(), and the host and the device may be reset at the
same time.

Only take the early path while pm_op_in_progress is set and a runtime
suspend or resume of the WLUN is in progress. The runtime PM core sets the
runtime status of the WLUN to RPM_SUSPENDING or RPM_RESUMING while
ufshcd_wl_runtime_suspend() or ufshcd_wl_runtime_resume() runs, and it is
RPM_ACTIVE or RPM_SUSPENDED during system PM. The runtime status alone is
not enough: it also covers the block layer steps before and after the
driver callbacks, where the early link recovery must not run.
pm_op_in_progress is only set while __ufshcd_wl_suspend() or
__ufshcd_wl_resume() run, which is inside that window.

Both checks are done in the new function ufshcd_in_wl_rpm_callback().  The
runtime status is only available with CONFIG_PM, so the function returns
false without it. Both values are read without locking, so use READ_ONCE()
for them and WRITE_ONCE() when pm_op_in_progress is updated. As the window
of pm_op_in_progress is contained in the runtime PM window, a stale value
of either one can only make the error handler take the regular path, like
an error handler that starts just before or after the PM operation.

For the other PM operations the regular error handling is safe:

  - the system PM callbacks hold host_sem from ufshcd_wl_suspend() until
    ufshcd_wl_resume() returns, and ufshcd_wl_poweroff() holds it as well,
    so the error handler waits for them;

  - during shutdown, hba->shutting_down makes the error handler stop.

This changes the behavior during shutdown: errors that occur while the
final START STOP UNIT command is being processed are no longer handled by
the error handler. Recovery then only happens through
ufshcd_eh_timed_out().

Fixes: e23ef4f22db3 ("scsi: ufs: core: Fix error handler host_sem issue")
Signed-off-by: HOYOUNG SEO <hy50.seo@samsung.com>
Reviewed-by: Peter Wang <peter.wang@mediatek.com>
Reviewed-by: Bart Van Assche <bvanassche@acm.org>
Link: https://patch.msgid.link/282821294.121794387787588.JavaMail.epsvc@epcpadp2new
Signed-off-by: Martin K. Petersen (Oracle) <mkp@kernel.org>

[mzak: picked for q91o (21 Nov gains plan) from linux-next/maintainer tree commit 7693e76c9f8b; mark C; replaces the early-recovery check of our queued is_sys_suspended form (Hoyoung Seo) with the runtime-PM-callback check; keeps master conditional clock-gating release]

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/ufs/core/ufshcd.c | 35 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++---------
 1 file changed, 26 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/ufs/core/ufshcd.c b/drivers/ufs/core/ufshcd.c
index 7ae6d265881f7..40b0084c1a393 100644
--- a/drivers/ufs/core/ufshcd.c
+++ b/drivers/ufs/core/ufshcd.c
@@ -7083,6 +7083,23 @@ static bool ufshcd_abort_all(struct ufs_hba *hba)
 	return ret != 0;
 }
 
+/*
+ * Whether a runtime PM callback of the WLUN runs __ufshcd_wl_suspend() or
+ * __ufshcd_wl_resume().
+ */
+static bool ufshcd_in_wl_rpm_callback(struct ufs_hba *hba)
+{
+#ifdef CONFIG_PM
+	enum rpm_status status =
+		READ_ONCE(hba->ufs_device_wlun->sdev_gendev.power.runtime_status);
+
+	return READ_ONCE(hba->pm_op_in_progress) &&
+	       (status == RPM_SUSPENDING || status == RPM_RESUMING);
+#else
+	return false;
+#endif
+}
+
 /**
  * ufshcd_err_handler - handle UFS errors that require s/w attention
  * @work: pointer to work structure
@@ -7113,13 +7130,13 @@ static void ufshcd_err_handler(struct work_struct *work)
 		 * happen if we tried to resume the device while a PM operation
 		 * is already in progress.
 		 *
-		 * During system resume, host_sem is held from
-		 * ufshcd_wl_suspend() until ufshcd_wl_resume() returns, so wait
-		 * for it below instead of recovering the link concurrently with
-		 * the resume path.
+		 * Do this only while the PM callbacks run for a runtime PM
+		 * operation. The system PM and poweroff callbacks hold
+		 * host_sem, and shutting_down makes the regular path below
+		 * stop, so it does not reset the link concurrently with them.
 		 */
 		ufshcd_rpm_get_noresume(hba);
-		if (hba->pm_op_in_progress && !hba->is_sys_suspended) {
+		if (ufshcd_in_wl_rpm_callback(hba)) {
 			ufshcd_link_recovery(hba);
 			ufshcd_rpm_put(hba);
 			return;
@@ -10430,7 +10447,7 @@ static int __ufshcd_wl_suspend(struct ufs_hba *hba, enum ufs_pm_op pm_op)
 	enum ufs_dev_pwr_mode req_dev_pwr_mode;
 	enum uic_link_state req_link_state;
 
-	hba->pm_op_in_progress = true;
+	WRITE_ONCE(hba->pm_op_in_progress, true);
 	if (pm_op != UFS_SHUTDOWN_PM) {
 		pm_lvl = pm_op == UFS_RUNTIME_PM ?
 			 hba->rpm_lvl : hba->spm_lvl;
@@ -10603,7 +10620,7 @@ static int __ufshcd_wl_suspend(struct ufs_hba *hba, enum ufs_pm_op pm_op)
 		hba->clk_gating.is_suspended = false;
 		ufshcd_release(hba);
 	}
-	hba->pm_op_in_progress = false;
+	WRITE_ONCE(hba->pm_op_in_progress, false);
 	return ret;
 }
 
@@ -10613,7 +10630,7 @@ static int __ufshcd_wl_resume(struct ufs_hba *hba, enum ufs_pm_op pm_op)
 	int ret;
 	enum uic_link_state old_link_state = hba->uic_link_state;
 
-	hba->pm_op_in_progress = true;
+	WRITE_ONCE(hba->pm_op_in_progress, true);
 
 	/*
 	 * Call vendor specific resume callback. As these callbacks may access
@@ -10710,7 +10727,7 @@ static int __ufshcd_wl_resume(struct ufs_hba *hba, enum ufs_pm_op pm_op)
 		hba->clk_gating.is_suspended = false;
 		ufshcd_release(hba);
 	}
-	hba->pm_op_in_progress = false;
+	WRITE_ONCE(hba->pm_op_in_progress, false);
 	return ret;
 }
 
